<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 920 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 920 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 920 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 420 million stg outright in bills maturing on or before July 14 and 500 million in repos to July 14.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 1.14 billion stg so far on Monday, in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.6 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
